From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flax <flax@tiogapass>
Date: Thu, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbtp: gate CPU/PCH VR voltage sensors on host power state

The CPU and PCH voltage-regulator rails (MB_VR_CPU*_*, MB_VR_PCH_*) are
unpowered while the host is off, so psusensor reads ~0 V and trips the
"Lower Non-critical going low" threshold, flooding the SEL with one
assertion per rail on every power-down and another on every power-up.
These are not real faults - the rails are simply off.

Add "PowerState": "On" to each VR pmbus block so psusensor only samples
and threshold-checks them while the host is powered on.  The hot-swap
controller (MB_HSC) is left ungated because its input rail is present
whenever the PSU/PDB is powered.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform configuration]
---
 configurations/fbtp.json | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

